Restore the arm-none-symbianelf target triple in binutils.

Upstream binutils retired `arm*-*-symbianelf*` (it sits in the obsolete-targets
list in bfd/config.bfd, and gas/ld never learned it back). GCC, however, still
carries the target: gcc/config.gcc maps `arm*-*-symbianelf*` to arm/symbian.h +
arm/t-symbian, which is what gives us __SYMBIAN32__, the Symbian dllimport/
dllexport semantics, and "don't assume GCC's libstdc++" behaviour. To build that
GCC we need a binutils that accepts the same triple.

We do NOT need to resurrect BFD's old `elf32-littlearm-symbian` vector. Its job
was to emit a program-header-less, postlinker-friendly image; in our pipeline
that role belongs to elf2e32, which reads a perfectly ordinary ARM ELF via
libelf and emits the E32Image itself. So we alias symbianelf onto the plain
little-endian ARM ELF/EABI configuration.

Three files, one line each.

--- a/bfd/config.bfd
+++ b/bfd/config.bfd
@@ -93,7 +93,6 @@
  arm*-*-netbsdaout* | \
  arm-*-oabi | \
  arm-*-riscix* | \
- arm*-*-symbianelf* | \
  arm-epoc-pe* | \
  c30-*-*aout* | tic30-*-*aout* | \
  cr16c-*-* | \
@@ -422,7 +421,7 @@
   arm-*-elf | arm*-*-freebsd* | arm*-*-linux-* | arm*-*-conix* | \
   arm*-*-uclinux* | arm-*-kfreebsd*-gnu | \
-  arm*-*-eabi* | arm-*-rtems* | arm*-*-uclinuxfdpiceabi)
+  arm*-*-eabi* | arm*-*-symbianelf* | arm-*-rtems* | arm*-*-uclinuxfdpiceabi)
     targ_defvec=arm_elf32_le_vec
     targ_selvecs="arm_elf32_be_vec arm_elf32_fdpic_le_vec arm_elf32_fdpic_be_vec"
     ;;

--- a/gas/configure.tgt
+++ b/gas/configure.tgt
@@ -151,7 +151,7 @@
   arm-*-phoenix*)			fmt=elf ;;
   arm-*-elf)				fmt=elf ;;
-  arm-*-eabi* | arm-*-rtems* | arm-*-genode*)	fmt=elf em=armeabi ;;
+  arm-*-eabi* | arm-*-symbianelf* | arm-*-rtems* | arm-*-genode*)	fmt=elf em=armeabi ;;

--- a/ld/configure.tgt
+++ b/ld/configure.tgt
@@ -206,1 +206,1 @@
-arm-*-elf | arm*-*-eabi* | arm-*-rtems* | arm-*-genode*)
+arm-*-elf | arm*-*-eabi* | arm*-*-symbianelf* | arm-*-rtems* | arm-*-genode*)
 			targ_emul=armelf
 			;;
